<h1>assessed entity</h1>
<p><code>gmeow:assessedEntity</code> · Property</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>CURIE</td><td><code>gmeow:assessedEntity</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>IRI</td><td><code>https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/assessedEntity</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Category</td><td>Property</td></tr>
<tr><td>Slice</td><td><a href="../../slices/quality/index.html">GMEOW Data Quality Module</a></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p><img src="../../badges/completeness/12.svg" alt="completeness: Docs 12/17" /> <img src="../../badges/stability/stable.svg" alt="stability: stable" /> <img src="../../badges/category/property.svg" alt="category: Property" /> <img src="../../badges/box/boxrbox.svg" alt="box: RBox" /> <img src="../../badges/stereotype/objectproperty.svg" alt="stereotype: ObjectProperty" /></p>
<h2>Definition</h2>
<p>The entity whose data quality is being assessed — the feature of interest of the quality observation. Sub-property of gmeow:observedFeature so generic consumers can query 'all observations about Alice' without knowing whether the claim is a name, a coordinate, or a quality assessment.</p>
<h2>For developers</h2>
<h2>Quickstart</h2>
<pre><code class="language-turtle">&lt;subject&gt; a gmeow:QualityAssessment ;
    gmeow:assessedEntity &lt;...&gt; .  # gmeow:Entity
</code></pre>
<h2>Example in multiple syntaxes</h2>
<p><strong>Turtle</strong></p>
<pre><code class="language-turtle">&lt;subject&gt; a gmeow:QualityAssessment ;
    gmeow:assessedEntity &lt;...&gt; .  # gmeow:Entity
</code></pre>
<p><strong>JSON-LD</strong></p>
<pre><code class="language-json">{
  "@context": {},
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@id": "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/example/subject",
      "@type": [
        {
          "@id": "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/QualityAssessment"
        }
      ],
      "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/assessedEntity": {
        "@id": "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/example/..."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre>
