<h2>Conformance examples</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Do:</strong> <code>tests/conformance-fixtures/per-axis-grade-carries-its-axis.ttl</code>
<ul>
<li>Two grade records name the two rubric axes that publish under one ISO dimension, each carrying gmeow:assessmentAxis alongside the identical gmeow:qualityDimension. Recording the axis as first-class data is the intended shape of a grade, so the union of the module with this fixture MUST validate clean: nothing in the rubric's owned surface restricts an assessment to one grade per dimension, and a slice that scored two axes publishing under one dimension would otherwise be unable to report both.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>See the <a href="../../fixtures/index.html">conformance fixtures index</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Usage Advice</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Example:</strong> ex:posAcc gmeow:assessedEntity ex:roadLayer .</li>
<li><strong>Use when:</strong> Use on a QualityAssessment to name the entity or dataset whose quality is under evaluation — the quality observation's feature of interest.</li>
<li><strong>Avoid when:</strong> Avoid for the assessment's numeric verdict (that is gmeow:observationResult) and for non-quality observations, which use gmeow:observedFeature directly.</li>
<li><strong>How to use:</strong> Assert gmeow:assessedEntity from the QualityAssessment to the subject entity; it specializes gmeow:observedFeature, so generic 'all observations about X' queries find it by inheritance.</li>
</ul>
